vant","tokens":["The","poster","was","designed","by","Lola."]},{"id":"en-b1-07-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"By nimani kiritadi?","answers":["the agent"],"explanation":"Bajaruvchini.","hint":"are collected / was cleaned; by + agent when relevant","options":["the agent","only the date","the new object"]},{"id":"en-b1-07-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["English is spoken in our club."],"explanation":"Passive uchun be + V3: Books are collected; The room was cleaned. Be zamonga va egaga mos. By bajaruvchini aytadi, lekin noma’lum yoki muhim bo‘lmasa tashlab ketiladi. Passive amal bajaruvchini taxmin qilishga ruxsat bermaydi. Active: students collect books. Passive: books are collected by students. Obyekt yangi gap egasiga aylanganda ma’no saqlansin.","hint":"are collected / was cleaned; by + agent when relevant","tokens":["English","is","spoken","in","our","club."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-08','en-b1-08',null,3,8,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-08","baseId":"en-b1-08","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":8,"title":"Reported speech va savollarni yetkazish","objective":"Boshqaning xabari va savolini bevosita iqtibossiz aytasiz.","context":"To‘garak rahbarining xabari kelmagan do‘stga yetkaziladi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-07"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas.","Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas.","Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang."],"pattern":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","examples":["She said she was ready.","He told me the room was closed.","Lola asked where I lived.","The teacher asked if we were ready.","Ali said he would call later.","She told us to bring notebooks."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-08-v0","term":"report","meaning":"yetkazmoq","ipa":"/rɪˈpɔːt/","collocation":"report a message","example":"Reporting a message is useful only if the new listener can understand what to do."},{"id":"en-b1-08-v1","term":"later","meaning":"keyinroq","ipa":"/ˈleɪtə/","collocation":"call later","example":"Ali said he would call later."},{"id":"en-b1-08-v2","term":"whether","meaning":"… yoki yo‘qmi","ipa":"/ˈweðə/","collocation":"ask whether","example":"Ali asked where the library entrance was and whether the meeting started at four."},{"id":"en-b1-08-v3","term":"remind","meaning":"eslatmoq","ipa":"/rɪˈmaɪnd/","collocation":"remind a friend","example":"remind a friend"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"dialogue","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","She said she was ready.","He told me the room was closed."]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["To‘garak rahbarining xabari kelmagan do‘stga yetkaziladi.","Lola asked where I lived.","Ali said he would call later."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"The teacher asked if we were ready.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-08-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-08-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reported questionni tanlang.","answers":["He asked if I was ready."],"explanation":"Gap tartibi I was.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["He asked if I was ready.","He asked was I ready?","He asked if was I ready."]},{"id":"en-b1-08-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She ___ me she was ready. (tell, past)","answers":["told"],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready"},{"id":"en-b1-08-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["She said she was ready."],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","tokens":["She","said","she","was","ready."]},{"id":"en-b1-08-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She asked where did I live.","answers":["She asked where I lived."],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready"},{"id":"en-b1-08-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["yetkazmoq","keyinroq","… yoki yo‘qmi","eslatmoq"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","left":["report","later","whether","remind"],"options":["yetkazmoq","keyinroq","… yoki yo‘qmi","eslatmoq"]},{"id":"en-b1-08-dialogue","type":"dialogue","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Sherik: “Can you give one example?” Siz: darsdagi birinchi namunani qayta tuzing.","answers":["She said she was ready."],"tokens":["She","said","she","was","ready."],"hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas."},{"id":"en-b1-08-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Kelajak uchrashuvlari va taxminlar: Jadvalni tanlang.","answers":["The train leaves at eight."],"explanation":"Train leaves — jadval.","hint":"train leaves / we’re meeting / going to prepare / will help / when I arrive","options":["The train leaves at eight.","I’ll carry your bag.","I think it will be useful."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Kelajak uchrashuvlari va taxminlar"},{"id":"en-b1-08-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · First va Second Conditional: real va xayoliy: Real ehtimol qaysi?","answers":["If we get funding, we will start."],"explanation":"Present + will real kelajak sharti.","hint":"If + present, will … / If + past, would …","options":["If we get funding, we will start.","If we had funding, we would start.","We started last year."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"First va Second Conditional: real va xayoliy"},{"id":"en-b1-08-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Passive: ish va natijaga e’tibor: Passive tuzilmasini tanlang.","answers":["Books are collected."],"explanation":"Be + V3.","hint":"are collected / was cleaned; by + agent when relevant","options":["Books are collected.","Books collected are students.","Books are collect."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Passive: ish va natijaga e’tibor"}],"reading":{"title":"Reported speech va savollarni yetkazish — vaziyat","text":"Ali missed the club meeting, so Lola sent him a summary. The teacher had said that Room 3 was closed and that the next meeting would be in the library. She had asked everyone to bring a notebook. Lola told Ali that they were preparing short talks about local places. Ali asked where the library entrance was and whether the meeting started at four. Lola explained that the entrance was near the park and that the meeting started at half past four. She did not repeat every sentence exactly, but she kept the important details. Before sending the message, she checked the time again. Ali thanked her and said he would prepare a photo for his talk. Reporting a message is useful only if the new listener can understand what to do.","sentences":["Ali missed the club meeting, so Lola sent him a summary.","The teacher had said that Room 3 was closed and that the next meeting would be in the library.","She had asked everyone to bring a notebook.","Lola told Ali that they were preparing short talks about local places.","Ali asked where the library entrance was and whether the meeting started at four.","Lola explained that the entrance was near the park and that the meeting started at half past four.","She did not repeat every sentence exactly, but she kept the important details.","Before sending the message, she checked the time again.","Ali thanked her and said he would prepare a photo for his talk.","Reporting a message is useful only if the new listener can understand what to do."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-08-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Uchrashuv nechada boshlanadi?","answers":["half past four"],"explanation":"Lola 4:30 deb aniqlashtiradi.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["half past four","four","five"]},{"id":"en-b1-08-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Nega hamma gap so‘zma-so‘z berilmagan?","answers":["a summary keeps important details"],"explanation":"Vazifa amaliy mazmunni yetkazish.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["a summary keeps important details","she forgot the entire message","reported speech forbids facts"]},{"id":"en-b1-08-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["Ali missed the club meeting, so Lola sent him a summary.","The teacher had said that Room 3 was closed and that the next meeting would be in the library.","She had asked everyone to bring a notebook.","Lola told Ali that they were preparing short talks about local places.","Ali asked where the library entrance was and whether the meeting started at four.","Lola explained that the entrance was near the park and that the meeting started at half past four.","She did not repeat every sentence exactly, but she kept the important details.","Before sending the message, she checked the time again.","Ali thanked her and said he would prepare a photo for his talk.","Reporting a message is useful only if the new listener can understand what to do."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"The teacher said the next meeting would be in the library. She told us to bring notebooks. Ali asked whether it started at four. Lola explained that it started at half past four, near the park entrance.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-08.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-08-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Nima olib kelish aytilgan?","answers":["notebooks"],"explanation":"Told us to bring notebooks.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["notebooks","food","tickets"]},{"id":"en-b1-08-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Soat qaysi?","answers":["4:30"],"explanation":"Half past four.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["4:30","4:00","5:30"]},{"id":"en-b1-08-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["library","4:30"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","rows":["Joy","Vaqt"]},{"id":"en-b1-08-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["The teacher asked if we were ready."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-08-dictation.mp3","transcript":"The teacher asked if we were ready."}]},"writing":{"task":"Ustozning xabarini kelmagan do‘stingizga muhim ma’lumotlarni saqlab yetkazing.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"Hi Ali, our teacher said that the next meeting would be in the library because Room 3 was closed. She told us to bring notebooks and asked us to prepare a short talk about a local place. You asked whether the meeting started at four. I checked again, and it starts at half past four. The entrance is near the park. The teacher also reminded us to choose one clear photo rather than many unrelated pictures. Please tell me if you need help finding the entrance. I can meet you outside ten minutes before the talk begins.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["She said she was ready.","He told me the room was closed.","Lola asked where I lived."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Qisqa xabarni tinglang va boshqa sherigingizga o‘z so‘zingiz bilan yetkazing.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Ustozning xabarini kelmagan do‘stingizga muhim ma’lumotlarni saqlab yetkazing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-08-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"He ___ me the room was closed.","answers":["told"],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready"},{"id":"en-b1-08-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She asked ___ we were ready.","answers":["if"],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready"},{"id":"en-b1-08-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ali said he ___ call later.","answers":["would"],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready"},{"id":"en-b1-08-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Say bilan qaysi gap to‘g‘ri?","answers":["She said she was ready."],"explanation":"Say + xabar.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["She said she was ready.","She said me ready.","She said to ready me."]},{"id":"en-b1-08-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reported savolda tartib qanday?","answers":["statement order"],"explanation":"Where I lived.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["statement order","inversion always","do/does always"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-08-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["He told me the room was closed."],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","tokens":["He","told","me","the","room","was","closed."]},{"id":"en-b1-08-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She asked ___ we were ready.","answers":["if"],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready"},{"id":"en-b1-08-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The teacher asked if we were ready."],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","tokens":["The","teacher","asked","if","we","were","ready."]},{"id":"en-b1-08-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Say bilan qaysi gap to‘g‘ri?","answers":["She said she was ready."],"explanation":"Say + xabar.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","options":["She said she was ready.","She said me ready.","She said to ready me."]},{"id":"en-b1-08-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["She told us to bring notebooks."],"explanation":"O‘tgan reporting fe’ldan keyin shakl ko‘pincha orqaga siljiydi: She said, “I am ready” → She said she was ready. Mazmun hali haqiqiy bo‘lsa har doim backshift shart emas. Say xabarni, tell odatda kimga aytilganini oladi: told me. Said me standart shakl emas. Reported questionda savol tartibi emas, gap tartibi: She asked where I lived. Yes/no savolda if/whether. Olmosh, vaqt va joyni haqiqiy vaziyatga moslang.","hint":"said that … / told me … / asked where I lived / asked if I was ready","tokens":["She","told","us","to","bring","notebooks."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied.","recapQuestions":[{"id":"en-b1-08-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Kelajak uchrashuvlari va taxminlar: Jadvalni tanlang.","answers":["The train leaves at eight."],"explanation":"Train leaves — jadval.","hint":"train leaves / we’re meeting / going to prepare / will help / when I arrive","options":["The train leaves at eight.","I’ll carry your bag.","I think it will be useful."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Kelajak uchrashuvlari va taxminlar"},{"id":"en-b1-08-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · First va Second Conditional: real va xayoliy: Real ehtimol qaysi?","answers":["If we get funding, we will start."],"explanation":"Present + will real kelajak sharti.","hint":"If + present, will … / If + past, would …","options":["If we get funding, we will start.","If we had funding, we would start.","We started last year."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"First va Second Conditional: real va xayoliy"},{"id":"en-b1-08-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Passive: ish va natijaga e’tibor: Passive tuzilmasini tanlang.","answers":["Books are collected."],"explanation":"Be + V3.","hint":"are collected / was cleaned; by + agent when relevant","options":["Books are collected.","Books collected are students.","Books are collect."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Passive: ish va natijaga e’tibor"}]}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-09','en-b1-09',null,3,9,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-09","baseId":"en-b1-09","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":9,"title":"Defining relative clauses","objective":"Qaysi odam yoki narsa nazarda tutilganini relative clause bilan aniqlashtirasiz.","context":"Yo‘qolgan narsalar stolida bir buyumni aniq tasvirlaysiz.","prerequisites":["en-b1-08"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi.","Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me.","Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang."],"pattern":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","examples":["The student who helped me is here.","This is the book that I borrowed.","I need a bag which has a strong handle.","That is the place where we met.","The pen I lost was blue.","People who read often learn new words."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-09-v0","term":"handle","meaning":"dasta","ipa":"/ˈhændəl/","collocation":"a strong handle","example":"I need a bag which has a strong handle."},{"id":"en-b1-09-v1","term":"identify","meaning":"aniqlamoq","ipa":"/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/","collocation":"identify an object","example":"These details identify my bag more clearly than simply saying it is blue."},{"id":"en-b1-09-v2","term":"borrow","meaning":"vaqtincha olmoq","ipa":"/ˈbɒrəʊ/","collocation":"the book I borrowed","example":"This is the book that I borrowed."},{"id":"en-b1-09-v3","term":"lost property","meaning":"yo‘qolgan-topilgan buyumlar","ipa":"/lɒst ˈprɒpəti/","collocation":"lost property desk","example":"She shows me a table where people can collect lost property."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"sentence","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","The student who helped me is here.","This is the book that I borrowed."]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["Yo‘qolgan narsalar stolida bir buyumni aniq tasvirlaysiz.","I need a bag which has a strong handle.","The pen I lost was blue."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"That is the place where we met.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-09-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-09-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ega relative olmoshi tushishi mumkinmi?","answers":["No, not in “the student who helped”."],"explanation":"Who bu yerda helped ning egasi.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["No, not in “the student who helped”.","Yes, always.","Only if it is a person."]},{"id":"en-b1-09-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The student ___ helped me is here.","answers":["who","that"],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met"},{"id":"en-b1-09-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["The student who helped me is here."],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","tokens":["The","student","who","helped","me","is","here."]},{"id":"en-b1-09-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The book that I borrowed it is new.","answers":["The book that I borrowed is new."],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met"},{"id":"en-b1-09-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["dasta","aniqlamoq","vaqtincha olmoq","yo‘qolgan-topilgan buyumlar"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","left":["handle","identify","borrow","lost property"],"options":["dasta","aniqlamoq","vaqtincha olmoq","yo‘qolgan-topilgan buyumlar"]},{"id":"en-b1-09-collocations","type":"collocation","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni darsdagi birikmasi bilan moslang.","left":["handle","identify","borrow","lost property"],"options":["a strong handle","identify an object","the book I borrowed","lost property desk"],"answers":["a strong handle","identify an object","the book I borrowed","lost property desk"],"hint":"So‘z qaysi birikmada ishlatilishini eslang.","explanation":"Birikmani yozgan gapingizda ham ishlating."}],"reading":{"title":"Defining relative clauses — vaziyat","text":"Several bags were left after the school exhibition. The bag that I lost has a small green label and a strong black handle. It is not the bag which has a picture of a bird. A student who helped at the entrance remembers where I put it. She shows me a table where people can collect lost property. On the table I see the book I borrowed from the library, but my bag is under a chair nearby. The assistant asks me to describe one item inside before returning it. I explain that there is a notebook which has my name on the first page. These details identify my bag more clearly than simply saying it is blue. A defining clause helps the listener know exactly which person, object or place I mean.","sentences":["Several bags were left after the school exhibition.","The bag that I lost has a small green label and a strong black handle.","It is not the bag which has a picture of a bird.","A student who helped at the entrance remembers where I put it.","She shows me a table where people can collect lost property.","On the table I see the book I borrowed from the library, but my bag is under a chair nearby.","The assistant asks me to describe one item inside before returning it.","I explain that there is a notebook which has my name on the first page.","These details identify my bag more clearly than simply saying it is blue.","A defining clause helps the listener know exactly which person, object or place I mean."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-09-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Qaysi sumka yo‘qolgan?","answers":["the one with a green label and black handle"],"explanation":"Defining tafsilotlar egani aniqlaydi.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["the one with a green label and black handle","the one with a bird picture","any bag on the table"]},{"id":"en-b1-09-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Nega qo‘shimcha detal so‘raladi?","answers":["to identify the owner more clearly"],"explanation":"Aniq identifikatsiya uchun.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["to identify the owner more clearly","to sell the bag","to change its colour"]},{"id":"en-b1-09-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["Several bags were left after the school exhibition.","The bag that I lost has a small green label and a strong black handle.","It is not the bag which has a picture of a bird.","A student who helped at the entrance remembers where I put it.","She shows me a table where people can collect lost property.","On the table I see the book I borrowed from the library, but my bag is under a chair nearby.","The assistant asks me to describe one item inside before returning it.","I explain that there is a notebook which has my name on the first page.","These details identify my bag more clearly than simply saying it is blue.","A defining clause helps the listener know exactly which person, object or place I mean."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"My bag has a green label and a black handle. It isn’t the one with a bird picture. The student who helped at the entrance saw it under a chair. My notebook has my name on the first page.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-09.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-09-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Yorliq rangi?","answers":["green"],"explanation":"Green label.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["green","blue","red"]},{"id":"en-b1-09-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Sumka qayerda?","answers":["under a chair"],"explanation":"Under a chair.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["under a chair","on a bus","inside a cupboard"]},{"id":"en-b1-09-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["green","black"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","rows":["Yorliq","Dasta"]},{"id":"en-b1-09-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["That is the place where we met."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-09-dictation.mp3","transcript":"That is the place where we met."}]},"writing":{"task":"Topilgan buyum yoki kerakli odamni uch aniq relative clause bilan tasvirlang.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"I am looking for the notebook that I left in the reading room. It has a green cover and a label which shows my name. The student who was sitting near the window may have seen it. I borrowed a book from the library, and I put the notebook beside it. The page I need contains notes for tomorrow’s talk. Please ask at the desk where students collect lost property. If you find the notebook, leave it with the teacher who manages our club. These details should help identify it without opening someone else’s private work.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["The student who helped me is here.","This is the book that I borrowed.","I need a bag which has a strong handle."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Bir buyumni boshqalardan farqlaydigan tafsilotlar bilan taniting.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Topilgan buyum yoki kerakli odamni uch aniq relative clause bilan tasvirlang.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-09-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The book ___ I borrowed is new.","answers":["that"],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met"},{"id":"en-b1-09-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The person ___ helped is Lola.","answers":["who"],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met"},{"id":"en-b1-09-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The place ___ we met is near school.","answers":["where"],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met"},{"id":"en-b1-09-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Obyekt olmoshni tushirish mumkin bo‘lgan gap?","answers":["the book I borrowed"],"explanation":"I borrowed bookda obyekt bo‘shlig‘i bor.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["the book I borrowed","the student helped me (same relative meaning)","the room is bright"]},{"id":"en-b1-09-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Defining qism odatda vergul oladimi?","answers":["No"],"explanation":"Identifikatsiya uchun zarur qism.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["No","Yes, always","Only after who"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-09-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["This is the book that I borrowed."],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","tokens":["This","is","the","book","that","I","borrowed."]},{"id":"en-b1-09-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The person ___ helped is Lola.","answers":["who"],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met"},{"id":"en-b1-09-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["That is the place where we met."],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","tokens":["That","is","the","place","where","we","met."]},{"id":"en-b1-09-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Obyekt olmoshni tushirish mumkin bo‘lgan gap?","answers":["the book I borrowed"],"explanation":"I borrowed bookda obyekt bo‘shlig‘i bor.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["the book I borrowed","the student helped me (same relative meaning)","the room is bright"]},{"id":"en-b1-09-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["People who read often learn new words."],"explanation":"Who odamlarga, which narsalarga, that ko‘pincha ikkalasiga ishlatiladi. Defining clause qaysi obyekt ekanini aniqlaydi. Olmosh obyekt bo‘lsa tushishi mumkin: the book (that) I borrowed. Ega bo‘lsa tushmaydi: the student who helped me. Bu aniqlovchi qism odatda vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Relative olmoshdan keyin qo‘shimcha takroriy it/he ishlatmang.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","tokens":["People","who","read","often","learn","new","words."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-10','en-b1-10',null,3,10,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-10","baseId":"en-b1-10","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":10,"title":"Modals: maslahat, ruxsat va ehtimol","objective":"Must, should, can va might ma’nolarini vaziyatga mos tanlaysiz.","context":"Loyiha uchun ustozga murojaat va safar noaniqligi muhokama qilinadi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-09"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim.","Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas.","Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang."],"pattern":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","examples":["She must be busy.","Ali might arrive late.","That can’t be Ali; he is away.","You should ask before using the room.","We can borrow the projector.","We mustn’t share private photos."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-10-v0","term":"evidence","meaning":"dalil","ipa":"/ˈevɪdəns/","collocation":"based on evidence","example":"based on evidence"},{"id":"en-b1-10-v1","term":"permission","meaning":"ruxsat","ipa":"/pəˈmɪʃən/","collocation":"ask permission","example":"When we receive permission, we check the room and agree not to use classmates’ private photos without asking them."},{"id":"en-b1-10-v2","term":"private","meaning":"shaxsiy","ipa":"/ˈpraɪvət/","collocation":"private photos","example":"We mustn’t share private photos."},{"id":"en-b1-10-v3","term":"busy","meaning":"band","ipa":"/ˈbɪzi/","collocation":"a busy teacher","example":"She must be busy."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"cause","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","She must be busy.","Ali might arrive late."]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["Loyiha uchun ustozga murojaat va safar noaniqligi muhokama qilinadi.","That can’t be Ali; he is away.","We can borrow the projector."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"You should ask before using the room.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-10-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-10-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Dalilga tayangan xulosani tanlang.","answers":["She must be busy; her meeting is still running."],"explanation":"Must be bu yerda deduction.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["She must be busy; her meeting is still running.","You mustn’t enter.","You should rest."]},{"id":"en-b1-10-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She ___ be busy. (ehtimol)","answers":["might","may"],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask"},{"id":"en-b1-10-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["She must be busy."],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","tokens":["She","must","be","busy."]},{"id":"en-b1-10-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She must to be busy.","answers":["She must be busy."],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask"},{"id":"en-b1-10-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["dalil","ruxsat","shaxsiy","band"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","left":["evidence","permission","private","busy"],"options":["dalil","ruxsat","shaxsiy","band"]}],"reading":{"title":"Modals: maslahat, ruxsat va ehtimol — vaziyat","text":"We want to show a short presentation in the library. We can borrow the projector, but we have to ask the teacher first. Lola says the teacher might be busy because she has two meetings today. Ali thinks we should send a clear message rather than interrupt her lesson. A student says that someone near the door must be our teacher. I reply that it can’t be her because she is teaching upstairs. We decide to wait for a reply. When we receive permission, we check the room and agree not to use classmates’ private photos without asking them. The teacher may attend our presentation, but she has not confirmed it. We therefore prepare a plan that works whether she comes or not. Different modal verbs help us separate rules, advice and uncertain information.","sentences":["We want to show a short presentation in the library.","We can borrow the projector, but we have to ask the teacher first.","Lola says the teacher might be busy because she has two meetings today.","Ali thinks we should send a clear message rather than interrupt her lesson.","A student says that someone near the door must be our teacher.","I reply that it can’t be her because she is teaching upstairs.","We decide to wait for a reply.","When we receive permission, we check the room and agree not to use classmates’ private photos without asking them.","The teacher may attend our presentation, but she has not confirmed it.","We therefore prepare a plan that works whether she comes or not.","Different modal verbs help us separate rules, advice and uncertain information."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-10-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Ustozning qatnashuvi aniqmi?","answers":["No, it is unconfirmed"],"explanation":"May attend va not confirmed noaniqlik.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["No, it is unconfirmed","Yes, she promised","She is forbidden"]},{"id":"en-b1-10-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Private photos qoidasining ma’nosi nima?","answers":["ask before sharing"],"explanation":"Ruxsat chegarasi.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["ask before sharing","all photos are public","sharing is always required"]},{"id":"en-b1-10-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["We want to show a short presentation in the library.","We can borrow the projector, but we have to ask the teacher first.","Lola says the teacher might be busy because she has two meetings today.","Ali thinks we should send a clear message rather than interrupt her lesson.","A student says that someone near the door must be our teacher.","I reply that it can’t be her because she is teaching upstairs.","We decide to wait for a reply.","When we receive permission, we check the room and agree not to use classmates’ private photos without asking them.","The teacher may attend our presentation, but she has not confirmed it.","We therefore prepare a plan that works whether she comes or not.","Different modal verbs help us separate rules, advice and uncertain information."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"We can borrow the projector, but we must ask permission. The teacher might be busy. She may attend, but she has not confirmed it. We mustn’t share private photos without asking.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-10.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-10-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Nima qarzga olinishi mumkin?","answers":["projector"],"explanation":"Borrow the projector.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["projector","a bus","tickets"]},{"id":"en-b1-10-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Qatnashuv holati qanday?","answers":["not confirmed"],"explanation":"Has not confirmed it.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["not confirmed","cancelled forever","certain"]},{"id":"en-b1-10-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["projector","permission"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","rows":["Jihoz","Kerakli narsa"]},{"id":"en-b1-10-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["You should ask before using the room."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-10-dictation.mp3","transcript":"You should ask before using the room."}]},"writing":{"task":"Loyiha uchun ruxsat, maslahat, ehtimol va dalilga tayangan bir xulosani ajratib yozing.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"We can borrow the school projector, but we must ask permission before using it. We should send the teacher a clear message with the place and time. She might be busy today, so we should not expect an immediate reply. The library must be available because its afternoon meeting has been cancelled, but we still need to confirm this. We mustn’t use private photos without asking the people in them. The teacher may attend our presentation, although that is not certain. We will prepare instructions for another organiser as well so that our plan does not depend on one person.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["She must be busy.","Ali might arrive late.","That can’t be Ali; he is away."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Bitta vaziyatda qoida, maslahat va taxminni turli modals bilan tushuntiring.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Loyiha uchun ruxsat, maslahat, ehtimol va dalilga tayangan bir xulosani ajratib yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-10-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"We ___ ask permission. (maslahat)","answers":["should"],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask"},{"id":"en-b1-10-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She ___ be busy. (ehtimol)","answers":["might"],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask"},{"id":"en-b1-10-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"That ___ be Ali; he is away.","answers":["can’t"],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask"},{"id":"en-b1-10-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Mustn’t ma’nosi?","answers":["prohibition"],"explanation":"Taqiq.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["prohibition","uncertain possibility","optional activity"]},{"id":"en-b1-10-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Might natijani kafolatlaydimi?","answers":["No"],"explanation":"Might noaniqlikni saqlaydi.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["No","Yes","Always"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-10-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Ali might arrive late."],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","tokens":["Ali","might","arrive","late."]},{"id":"en-b1-10-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She ___ be busy. (ehtimol)","answers":["might"],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask"},{"id":"en-b1-10-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["You should ask before using the room."],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","tokens":["You","should","ask","before","using","the","room."]},{"id":"en-b1-10-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Mustn’t ma’nosi?","answers":["prohibition"],"explanation":"Taqiq.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["prohibition","uncertain possibility","optional activity"]},{"id":"en-b1-10-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["We mustn’t share private photos."],"explanation":"Should maslahat; must/have to kuchli zarurat; can ruxsat yoki imkoniyat. Bir shakl bir necha ma’no olishi mumkin, shuning uchun vaziyat muhim. Might/may ehtimol, must xulosa uchun ham ishlatiladi: She must be busy — dalilga tayangan taxmin, bu buyruq emas. Can’t deduction kuchli mumkin emas degan xulosa: That can’t be Ali; he is away. Mustn’t esa taqiq. Taxminni fakt sifatida sotmang.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","tokens":["We","mustn’t","share","private","photos."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","le