himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b2-07","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b2-08','en-b2-08',null,4,8,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b2-08","baseId":"en-b2-08","revision":1,"level":"B2","levelIndex":4,"order":8,"title":"Passive: jarayonni markazga qo‘yish","objective":"Murakkab passive zamonlarini hisobot maqsadiga mos qo‘llaysiz.","context":"Passive: jarayonni markazga qo‘yish","prerequisites":["en-b2-07"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi.","Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish.","Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang."],"pattern":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","examples":["The roof is being repaired.","The main room has been inspected.","The remaining windows will be checked.","The report was written by the engineer.","The building had been closed before the visit.","Safety rules must be followed."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b2-08-v0","term":"inspect","meaning":"tekshirmoq","ipa":"/ɪnˈspekt/","collocation":"inspect a building","example":"The main room has been inspected."},{"id":"en-b2-08-v1","term":"responsibility","meaning":"mas’uliyat","ipa":"/rɪˌspɒnsəˈbɪləti/","collocation":"take responsibility","example":"An effective report can focus on processes while still making responsibility clear."},{"id":"en-b2-08-v2","term":"maintenance","meaning":"texnik qarov","ipa":"/ˈmeɪntənəns/","collocation":"regular maintenance","example":"The manager adds the maintenance team’s name and a review date."},{"id":"en-b2-08-v3","term":"agent","meaning":"bajaruvchi","ipa":"/ˈeɪdʒənt/","collocation":"name the agent","example":"Parents ask for a contact person, not because every sentence needs an agent, but because someone must answer questions."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","The roof is being repaired.","The main room has been inspected."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["The hall is not ready to reopen.","Inspection is complete, but repairs continue.","Name the contact and the next review date."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"The report was written by the engineer.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-08-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b2-08-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: The roof is being ___. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["repaired","repairing","repair"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The roof is being ___. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked"},{"id":"en-b2-08-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["The roof is being repaired."],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","tokens":["The","roof","is","being","repaired."]},{"id":"en-b2-08-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The roof is being repair.","answers":["The roof is being repaired."],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked"},{"id":"en-b2-08-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["tekshirmoq","mas’uliyat","texnik qarov","bajaruvchi"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","left":["inspect","responsibility","maintenance","agent"],"options":["tekshirmoq","mas’uliyat","texnik qarov","bajaruvchi"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Passive: The engineer has inspected the hall.","answers":["The hall has been inspected by the engineer."],"hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi."},{"id":"en-b2-08-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["The hall is not ready to reopen.","Inspection is complete, but repairs continue.","Name the contact and the next review date."],"answers":["The hall is not ready to reopen.\nInspection is complete, but repairs continue.\nName the contact and the next review date."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."},{"id":"en-b2-08-dialogue","type":"dialogue","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Sherik: “Can you give one example?” Siz: darsdagi birinchi namunani qayta tuzing.","answers":["The roof is being repaired."],"tokens":["The","roof","is","being","repaired."],"hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi."},{"id":"en-b2-08-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Wish va if only: Til vositasini tanlang: I wish we ___ checked earlier.","answers":["had"],"explanation":"Wish + past simple hozirgi boshqa holat istagi: I wish the room were quieter. Wish + had + V3 o‘tgan ishga afsus: I wish we had booked earlier. Wish + would boshqa odamning o‘zgarishi kutilgan xatti-harakatiga; oddiy o‘z qobiliyatingiz uchun could yoki past shakli.","hint":"wish were / wish had booked / wish would stop","options":["had","have","has"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Wish va if only"},{"id":"en-b2-08-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Would rather va had better: Til vositasini tanlang: I would rather ___ now. (practise)","answers":["practise"],"explanation":"Would rather + V afzallik; boshqa ega bilan would rather + subject + past simple. Had better + V vaziyatga bog‘liq kuchli maslahat; salbiy oqibat ehtimoli bor. Had better not; would rather not. Had better o‘tgan zamon emas va would rather bilan bir xil kuchda emas.","hint":"would rather practise / would rather you checked / had better save","options":["practise","practising","practised"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Would rather va had better"},{"id":"en-b2-08-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Past modals: dalil, ehtimol va tanqid: Til vositasini tanlang: She might have ___ another bus. (take)","answers":["taken"],"explanation":"Must have + V3 kuchli xulosa, might have ehtimol. Can’t have dalilga zid natijani rad etadi; should have o‘tgan maslahat yoki tanqid. Didn’t need to bilan needn’t have done bir xil emas: ikkinchisida ish bajarilgan.","hint":"must have / might have / should have + V3","options":["taken","take","taking"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Past modals: dalil, ehtimol va tanqid"}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"The sports hall has been inspected, and the roof is being repaired. A public notice says that the remaining windows will be checked before reopening. Passive forms keep attention on the building and the sequence of work. However, the notice also says that a mistake was made without naming who will correct it. Parents ask for a contact person, not because every sentence needs an agent, but because someone must answer questions. The manager adds the maintenance team’s name and a review date. An effective report can focus on processes while still making responsibility clear. Avoiding an agent is reasonable when the person is unknown or irrelevant; it is less helpful when readers need to know who can act.","sentences":["The sports hall has been inspected, and the roof is being repaired.","A public notice says that the remaining windows will be checked before reopening.","Passive forms keep attention on the building and the sequence of work.","However, the notice also says that a mistake was made without naming who will correct it.","Parents ask for a contact person, not because every sentence needs an agent, but because someone must answer questions.","The manager adds the maintenance team’s name and a review date.","An effective report can focus on processes while still making responsibility clear.","Avoiding an agent is reasonable when the person is unknown or irrelevant; it is less helpful when readers need to know who can act."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-08-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Passive nima uchun foydali?","answers":["it focuses on the work sequence"],"explanation":"Jarayon markazda.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["it focuses on the work sequence","it proves nobody is responsible","it removes every agent"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Parents nega kontakt so‘radi?","answers":["they needed someone who could act"],"explanation":"Mas’uliyat amaliy muhim.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["they needed someone who could act","they wanted grammar rules","all repairs were finished"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["The sports hall has been inspected, and the roof is being repaired.","A public notice says that the remaining windows will be checked before reopening.","Passive forms keep attention on the building and the sequence of work.","However, the notice also says that a mistake was made without naming who will correct it.","Parents ask for a contact person, not because every sentence needs an agent, but because someone must answer questions.","The manager adds the maintenance team’s name and a review date.","An effective report can focus on processes while still making responsibility clear.","Avoiding an agent is reasonable when the person is unknown or irrelevant; it is less helpful when readers need to know who can act."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is maintenance. The sports hall has been inspected, and the roof is being repaired. A public notice says that the remaining windows will be checked before reopening. Speaker two: My main point is responsibility. Readers need a clear contact as well as a process description. The sports hall has been inspected, and the roof is being repaired. A public notice says that the remaining windows will be checked before reopening. Passive forms keep attention on the building and the sequence of work. However, the notice also says that a mistake was made without naming who will correct it. Parents ask for a contact person, not because every sentence needs an agent, but because someone must answer questions. The manager adds the maintenance team’s name and a review date. An effective report can focus on processes while still making responsibility clear. Avoiding an agent is reasonable when the person is unknown or irrelevant; it is less helpful when readers need to know who can act.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-08.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-08-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Passive nima uchun foydali?","answers":["it focuses on the work sequence"],"explanation":"Jarayon markazda.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["it focuses on the work sequence","it proves nobody is responsible","it removes every agent"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Parents nega kontakt so‘radi?","answers":["they needed someone who could act"],"explanation":"Mas’uliyat amaliy muhim.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["they needed someone who could act","they wanted grammar rules","all repairs were finished"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["maintenance","responsibility"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["The report was written by the engineer."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-08-dictation.mp3","transcript":"The report was written by the engineer."}]},"writing":{"task":"Ta’mirlash hisobotida ish holati va mas’ul aloqani aniq yozing.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":320,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"The hall has been inspected, and the roof is being repaired by the maintenance team. The remaining windows will be checked before the hall reopens. The process is not yet complete, so students should continue using the smaller room. Questions can be sent to the building manager, who will publish a new review date on Friday. This report focuses on work completed and work in progress while giving readers a clear contact. A process description should not leave responsibility unclear.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["The roof is being repaired.","The main room has been inspected.","The remaining windows will be checked."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Ta’mirlash hisobotida ish holati va mas’ul aloqani aniq yozing. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":100,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Ta’mirlash hisobotida ish holati va mas’ul aloqani aniq yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b2-08-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The roof is being ___. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked"},{"id":"en-b2-08-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The room has ___ inspected.","answers":["been"],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked"},{"id":"en-b2-08-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Rules must be ___. (follow)","answers":["followed"],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked"},{"id":"en-b2-08-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Passive nima uchun foydali?","answers":["it focuses on the work sequence"],"explanation":"Jarayon markazda.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["it focuses on the work sequence","it proves nobody is responsible","it removes every agent"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Parents nega kontakt so‘radi?","answers":["they needed someone who could act"],"explanation":"Mas’uliyat amaliy muhim.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["they needed someone who could act","they wanted grammar rules","all repairs were finished"]}],[{"id":"en-b2-08-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The main room has been inspected."],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","tokens":["The","main","room","has","been","inspected."]},{"id":"en-b2-08-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The room has ___ inspected.","answers":["been"],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked"},{"id":"en-b2-08-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The report was written by the engineer."],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","tokens":["The","report","was","written","by","the","engineer."]},{"id":"en-b2-08-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Passive nima uchun foydali?","answers":["it focuses on the work sequence"],"explanation":"Jarayon markazda.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","options":["it focuses on the work sequence","it proves nobody is responsible","it removes every agent"]},{"id":"en-b2-08-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Safety rules must be followed."],"explanation":"Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi. Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish. Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.","hint":"is being checked / has been checked / will be checked","tokens":["Safety","rules","must","be","followed."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b2-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b2-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b2-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b2-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b2-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b2-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b2-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b2-08","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied.","recapQuestions":[{"id":"en-b2-08-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Wish va if only: Til vositasini tanlang: I wish we ___ checked earlier.","answers":["had"],"explanation":"Wish + past simple hozirgi boshqa holat istagi: I wish the room were quieter. Wish + had + V3 o‘tgan ishga afsus: I wish we had booked earlier. Wish + would boshqa odamning o‘zgarishi kutilgan xatti-harakatiga; oddiy o‘z qobiliyatingiz uchun could yoki past shakli.","hint":"wish were / wish had booked / wish would stop","options":["had","have","has"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Wish va if only"},{"id":"en-b2-08-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Would rather va had better: Til vositasini tanlang: I would rather ___ now. (practise)","answers":["practise"],"explanation":"Would rather + V afzallik; boshqa ega bilan would rather + subject + past simple. Had better + V vaziyatga bog‘liq kuchli maslahat; salbiy oqibat ehtimoli bor. Had better not; would rather not. Had better o‘tgan zamon emas va would rather bilan bir xil kuchda emas.","hint":"would rather practise / would rather you checked / had better save","options":["practise","practising","practised"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Would rather va had better"},{"id":"en-b2-08-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Past modals: dalil, ehtimol va tanqid: Til vositasini tanlang: She might have ___ another bus. (take)","answers":["taken"],"explanation":"Must have + V3 kuchli xulosa, might have ehtimol. Can’t have dalilga zid natijani rad etadi; should have o‘tgan maslahat yoki tanqid. Didn’t need to bilan needn’t have done bir xil emas: ikkinchisida ish bajarilgan.","hint":"must have / might have / should have + V3","options":["taken","take","taking"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Past modals: dalil, ehtimol va tanqid"}]}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b2-09','en-b2-09',null,4,9,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b2-09","baseId":"en-b2-09","revision":1,"level":"B2","levelIndex":4,"order":9,"title":"Reporting passive","objective":"Xabar manbasini faktning o‘zidan ajratib ko‘rsatasiz.","context":"Reporting passive","prerequisites":["en-b2-08"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi.","Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved.","Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating."],"pattern":"It is reported that / is believed to have","examples":["It is reported that the centre will reopen.","The centre is expected to reopen in May.","The organiser is said to have changed the plan.","The figures are believed to be incomplete.","It was announced that entry would be free.","The team is thought to have consulted residents."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b2-09-v0","term":"reportedly","meaning":"xabarlarga ko‘ra","ipa":"/rɪˈpɔːtɪdli/","collocation":"reportedly reopened","example":"reportedly reopened"},{"id":"en-b2-09-v1","term":"source","meaning":"manba","ipa":"/sɔːs/","collocation":"a named source","example":"A local article names the manager as its source, but an online post repeats the claim without that detail."},{"id":"en-b2-09-v2","term":"confirm","meaning":"tasdiqlamoq","ipa":"/kənˈfɜːm/","collocation":"confirm a date","example":"No official notice confirms the rules yet."},{"id":"en-b2-09-v3","term":"rumour","meaning":"mish-mish","ipa":"/ˈruːmə/","collocation":"an unconfirmed rumour","example":"an unconfirmed rumour"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["It is reported that / is believed to have","It is reported that the centre will reopen.","The centre is expected to reopen in May."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["A report announces a reopening plan.","The rule change lacks a named source.","Separate reported plans from confirmed events."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"The figures are believed to be incomplete.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-09-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b2-09-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: The centre is expected ___ reopen.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["to","for","at"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The centre is expected ___ reopen.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have"},{"id":"en-b2-09-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["It is reported that the centre will reopen."],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","tokens":["It","is","reported","that","the","centre","will","reopen."]},{"id":"en-b2-09-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The centre is said have changed its rules.","answers":["The centre is said to have changed its rules."],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have"},{"id":"en-b2-09-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["xabarlarga ko‘ra","manba","tasdiqlamoq","mish-mish"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","left":["reportedly","source","confirm","rumour"],"options":["xabarlarga ko‘ra","manba","tasdiqlamoq","mish-mish"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reporting passive: People believe the figures are incomplete.","answers":["The figures are believed to be incomplete."],"hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi."},{"id":"en-b2-09-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["A report announces a reopening plan.","The rule change lacks a named source.","Separate reported plans from confirmed events."],"answers":["A report announces a reopening plan.\nThe rule change lacks a named source.\nSeparate reported plans from confirmed events."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."},{"id":"en-b2-09-collocations","type":"collocation","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni darsdagi birikmasi bilan moslang.","left":["reportedly","source","confirm","rumour"],"options":["reportedly reopened","a named source","confirm a date","an unconfirmed rumour"],"answers":["reportedly reopened","a named source","confirm a date","an unconfirmed rumour"],"hint":"So‘z qaysi birikmada ishlatilishini eslang.","explanation":"Birikmani yozgan gapingizda ham ishlating."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"It is reported that the community centre will reopen in May. A local article names the manager as its source, but an online post repeats the claim without that detail. The centre is also said to have changed its entry rules. No official notice confirms the rules yet. Students compare the reports and find that the reopening date comes from one interview, while the rule change began as an unnamed comment. Reporting passive is useful because it signals that information is attributed to someone. It does not show whether the source is reliable. Before publishing their own summary, the students contact the centre and label the unconfirmed detail clearly. A careful summary distinguishes a reported plan from a completed or guaranteed event.","sentences":["It is reported that the community centre will reopen in May.","A local article names the manager as its source, but an online post repeats the claim without that detail.","The centre is also said to have changed its entry rules.","No official notice confirms the rules yet.","Students compare the reports and find that the reopening date comes from one interview, while the rule change began as an unnamed comment.","Reporting passive is useful because it signals that information is attributed to someone.","It does not show whether the source is reliable.","Before publishing their own summary, the students contact the centre and label the unconfirmed detail clearly.","A careful summary distinguishes a reported plan from a completed or guaranteed event."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-09-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Reopening date manbasi?","answers":["one interview with the manager"],"explanation":"Maqola bitta interviewga tayangan.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["one interview with the manager","a completed reopening","several independent reports"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Reporting passive nimani kafolatlamaydi?","answers":["source reliability"],"explanation":"Ishonchlilikni alohida tekshirish kerak.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["source reliability","attribution","a reporting structure"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["It is reported that the community centre will reopen in May.","A local article names the manager as its source, but an online post repeats the claim without that detail.","The centre is also said to have changed its entry rules.","No official notice confirms the rules yet.","Students compare the reports and find that the reopening date comes from one interview, while the rule change began as an unnamed comment.","Reporting passive is useful because it signals that information is attributed to someone.","It does not show whether the source is reliable.","Before publishing their own summary, the students contact the centre and label the unconfirmed detail clearly.","A careful summary distinguishes a reported plan from a completed or guaranteed event."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is source. It is reported that the community centre will reopen in May. A local article names the manager as its source, but an online post repeats the claim without that detail. Speaker two: My main point is confirmation. Attribution is useful, but unconfirmed rules need checking. It is reported that the community centre will reopen in May. A local article names the manager as its source, but an online post repeats the claim without that detail. The centre is also said to have changed its entry rules. No official notice confirms the rules yet. Students compare the reports and find that the reopening date comes from one interview, while the rule change began as an unnamed comment. Reporting passive is useful because it signals that information is attributed to someone. It does not show whether the source is reliable. Before publishing their own summary, the students contact the centre and label the unconfirmed detail clearly. A careful summary distinguishes a reported plan from a completed or guaranteed event.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-09.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-09-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Reopening date manbasi?","answers":["one interview with the manager"],"explanation":"Maqola bitta interviewga tayangan.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["one interview with the manager","a completed reopening","several independent reports"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Reporting passive nimani kafolatlamaydi?","answers":["source reliability"],"explanation":"Ishonchlilikni alohida tekshirish kerak.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["source reliability","attribution","a reporting structure"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["source","confirmation"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["The figures are believed to be incomplete."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-09-dictation.mp3","transcript":"The figures are believed to be incomplete."}]},"writing":{"task":"Ikki xabarni tekshirib, tasdiqlangan va taxminiy qismlar ajratilgan yangilik summarysi yozing.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":320,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"The centre is expected to reopen in May, according to an interview with its manager. This is a reported plan, rather than evidence that the building has already reopened. A separate claim about entry rules remains unconfirmed. The online post repeating it does not name an original source. We recommend checking the centre’s official notice before making travel plans. Our summary therefore keeps the reopening report and the uncertain rule change separate, so that readers can judge how strongly each detail is supported.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["It is reported that the centre will reopen.","The centre is expected to reopen in May.","The organiser is said to have changed the plan."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Ikki xabarni tekshirib, tasdiqlangan va taxminiy qismlar ajratilgan yangilik summarysi yozing. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":100,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Ikki xabarni tekshirib, tasdiqlangan va taxminiy qismlar ajratilgan yangilik summarysi yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b2-09-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The centre is expected ___ reopen.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have"},{"id":"en-b2-09-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The plan is said to have ___. (change)","answers":["changed"],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have"},{"id":"en-b2-09-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"It is ___ that entry will be free. (report)","answers":["reported"],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have"},{"id":"en-b2-09-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reopening date manbasi?","answers":["one interview with the manager"],"explanation":"Maqola bitta interviewga tayangan.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["one interview with the manager","a completed reopening","several independent reports"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reporting passive nimani kafolatlamaydi?","answers":["source reliability"],"explanation":"Ishonchlilikni alohida tekshirish kerak.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["source reliability","attribution","a reporting structure"]}],[{"id":"en-b2-09-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The centre is expected to reopen in May."],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","tokens":["The","centre","is","expected","to","reopen","in","May."]},{"id":"en-b2-09-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The plan is said to have ___. (change)","answers":["changed"],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have"},{"id":"en-b2-09-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The figures are believed to be incomplete."],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","tokens":["The","figures","are","believed","to","be","incomplete."]},{"id":"en-b2-09-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reopening date manbasi?","answers":["one interview with the manager"],"explanation":"Maqola bitta interviewga tayangan.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["one interview with the manager","a completed reopening","several independent reports"]},{"id":"en-b2-09-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The team is thought to have consulted residents."],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","tokens":["The","team","is","thought","to","have","consulted","residents."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b2-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b2-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b2-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b2-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b2-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b2-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b2-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b2-09","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b2-10','en-b2-10',null,4,10,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b2-10","baseId":"en-b2-10","revision":1,"level":"B2","levelIndex":4,"order":10,"title":"Causative have va get","objective":"Xizmatni o‘zi bajarish va boshqaga bajartirishni farqlaysiz.","context":"Causative have va get","prerequisites":["en-b2-09"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan.","Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi.","Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas."],"pattern":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","examples":["I had my laptop repaired.","We got the printer checked.","She had a technician install the update.","I got my brother to test the microphone.","He had his bag stolen on the bus.","Will you have the report printed?"],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b2-10-v0","term":"technician","meaning":"texnik mutaxassis","ipa":"/tekˈnɪʃən/","collocation":"a qualified technician","example":"She had a technician install the update."},{"id":"en-b2-10-v1","term":"service","meaning":"xizmat","ipa":"/ˈsɜːvɪs/","collocation":"book a service","example":"Ali arranged the service but did not diagnose the machine."},{"id":"en-b2-10-v2","term":"arrange","meaning":"tashkil qilmoq","ipa":"/əˈreɪndʒ/","collocation":"arrange a repair","example":"Ali arranged the service but did not diagnose the machine."},{"id":"en-b2-10-v3","term":"warranty","meaning":"kafolat","ipa":"/ˈwɒrənti/","collocation":"check the warranty","example":"The club checks the warranty before paying and asks the technician for a short written record."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["have a device repaired / get someone to check it","I had my laptop repaired.","We got the printer checked."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["The printer needs professional inspection.","The club must check warranty and cost.","Arrange the service and request a record."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"I got my brother to test the microphone.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-10-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b2-10-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: I had my laptop ___. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["repaired","repairing","repair"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I had my laptop ___. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it"},{"id":"en-b2-10-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["I had my laptop repaired."],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","tokens":["I","had","my","laptop","repaired."]},{"id":"en-b2-10-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I got him test the microphone.","answers":["I got him to test the microphone."],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it"},{"id":"en-b2-10-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["texnik mutaxassis","xizmat","tashkil qilmoq","kafolat"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","left":["technician","service","arrange","warranty"],"options":["texnik mutaxassis","xizmat","tashkil qilmoq","kafolat"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Xizmat: A technician repaired my laptop for me.","answers":["I had my laptop repaired."],"hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan."},{"id":"en-b2-10-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["The printer needs professional inspection.","The club must check warranty and cost.","Arrange the service and request a record."],"answers":["The printer needs professional inspection.\nThe club must check warranty and cost.\nArrange the service and request a record."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"The club printer stopped working before a display was due. Ali said he had repaired it, which sounded as if he had done the technical work himself. He actually had it repaired by a local technician. The distinction matters when the teacher asks who can explain the fault. Ali arranged the service but did not diagnose the machine. The club checks the warranty before paying and asks the technician for a short written record. Later, another student says she had her bag stolen on the bus. This has the same broad grammatical shape, but she did not arrange the action. Context determines whether the structure describes a service or an unwanted experience. Clear wording prevents mistaken assumptions about skills and responsibility.","sentences":["The club printer stopped working before a display was due.","Ali said he had repaired it, which sounded as if he had done the technical work himself.","He actually had it repaired by a local technician.","The distinction matters when the teacher asks who can explain the fault.","Ali arranged the service but did not diagnose the machine.","The club checks the warranty before paying and asks the technician for a short written record.","Later, another student says she had her bag stolen on the bus.","This has the same broad grammatical shape, but she did not arrange the action.","Context determines whether the structure describes a service or an unwanted experience.","Clear wording prevents mistaken assumptions about skills and responsibility."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-10-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Ali aslida nima qilgan?","answers":["arranged a repair"],"explanation":"Had it repaired xizmat.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["arranged a repair","diagnosed every fault himself","stole a bag"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Bag stolen nimani anglatadi?","answers":["an unwanted experience"],"explanation":"Kontekst buyurtma emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["an unwanted experience","a booked service","a repair request"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["The club printer stopped working before a display was due.","Ali said he had repaired it, which sounded as if he had done the technical work himself.","He actually had it repaired by a local technician.","The distinction matters when the teacher asks who can explain the fault.","Ali arranged the service but did not diagnose the machine.","The club checks the warranty before paying and asks the technician for a short written record.","Later, another student says she had her bag stolen on the bus.","This has the same broad grammatical shape, but she did not arrange the action.","Context determines whether the structure describes a service or an unwanted experience.","Clear wording prevents mistaken assumptions about skills and responsibility."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is service. The club printer stopped working before a display was due. Ali said he had repaired it, which sounded as if he had done the technical work himself. Speaker two: My main point is context. The same form can describe an arranged service or an unwanted experience. The club printer stopped working before a display was due. Ali said he had repaired it, which sounded as if he had done the technical work himself. He actually had it repaired by a local technician. The distinction matters when the teacher asks who can explain the fault. Ali arranged the service but did not diagnose the machine. The club checks the warranty before paying and asks the technician for a short written record. Later, another student says she had her bag stolen on the bus. This has the same broad grammatical shape, but she did not arrange the action. Context determines whether the structure describes a service or an unwanted experience. Clear wording prevents mistaken assumptions about skills and responsibility.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-10.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-10-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Ali aslida nima qilgan?","answers":["arranged a repair"],"explanation":"Had it repaired xizmat.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["arranged a repair","diagnosed every fault himself","stole a bag"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Bag stolen nimani anglatadi?","answers":["an unwanted experience"],"explanation":"Kontekst buyurtma emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["an unwanted experience","a booked service","a repair request"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["service","context"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["I got my brother to test the microphone."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-10-dictation.mp3","transcript":"I got my brother to test the microphone."}]},"writing":{"task":"Ta’mir xizmatini so‘rash uchun muammo, muddat va kafolat haqidagi email yozing.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":320,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"Dear technician, our club would like to have its printer checked before Friday. It stopped working during a print job, and we have not tried to open it ourselves. Could you explain the likely inspection time and whether the service is covered by the warranty? We need a written record of any work carried out. I am arranging the repair on behalf of the club, so please contact me before replacing parts. This will help us understand the cost and keep responsibility clear.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["I had my laptop repaired.","We got the printer checked.","She had a technician install the update."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Ta’mir xizmatini so‘rash uchun muammo, muddat va kafolat haqidagi email yozing. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":100,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Ta’mir xizmatini so‘rash uchun muammo, muddat va kafolat haqidagi email yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b2-10-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I had my laptop ___. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it"},{"id":"en-b2-10-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I got him ___ test the microphone.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it"},{"id":"en-b2-10-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She had a technician ___ the update. (install)","answers":["install"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it"},{"id":"en-b2-10-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ali aslida nima qilgan?","answers":["arranged a repair"],"explanation":"Had it repaired xizmat.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["arranged a repair","diagnosed every fault himself","stole a bag"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Bag stolen nimani anglatadi?","answers":["an unwanted experience"],"explanation":"Kontekst buyurtma emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["an unwanted experience","a booked service","a repair request"]}],[{"id":"en-b2-10-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["We got the printer checked."],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","tokens":["We","got","the","printer","checked."]},{"id":"en-b2-10-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I got him ___ test the microphone.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it"},{"id":"en-b2-10-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["I got my brother to test the microphone."],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","tokens":["I","got","my","brother","to","test","the","microphone."]},{"id":"en-b2-10-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ali aslida nima qilgan?","answers":["arranged a repair"],"explanation":"Had it repaired xizmat.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["arranged a repair","diagnosed every fault himself","stole a bag"]},{"id":"en-b2-10-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Will you have the report printed?"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","tokens":["Will","you","have","the","report","printed?"]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b2-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b2-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b2-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b2-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b2-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b2-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b2-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b2-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b2-11','en-b2-11',null,4,11,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b2-11","baseId":"en-b2-11","revision":1,"level":"B2","levelIndex":4,"order":11,"title":"Reporting verbs va mas’uliyat","objective":"Deny, admit, suggest va warn qoliplarini ma’noga mos tanlaysiz.","context":"Reporting verbs va mas’uliyat","prerequisites":["en-b2-10"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause.","Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing.","Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak."],"pattern":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","examples":["She admitted changing the date.","He denied sharing the file.","They suggested checking the records.","The teacher warned us not to publish names.","I agreed to correct the notice.","She apologised for sending the wrong link."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b2-11-v0","term":"admit","meaning":"tan olmoq","ipa":"/ədˈmɪt/","collocation":"admit a mistake","example":"She admitted changing the date."},{"id":"en-b2-11-v1","term":"deny","meaning":"rad etmoq","ipa":"/dɪˈnaɪ/","collocation":"deny sharing","example":"deny sharing"},{"id":"en-b2-11-v2","term":"clarify","meaning":"aniqlashtirmoq","ipa":"/ˈklærɪfaɪ/","collocation":"clarify a statement","example":"clarify a statement"},{"id":"en-b2-11-v3","term":"account","meaning":"bayon","ipa":"/əˈkaʊnt/","collocation":"a fair account","example":"The revised account separates acknowledged mistakes, suggestions, and disputed claims rather than turning all of them into confessions."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","She admitted changing the date.","He denied sharing the file."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["The original verb distorted the statement.","The recording supports more neutral wording.","Preserve intention when reporting speech."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"The teacher warned us not to publish names.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-11-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b2-11-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: She admitted ___ the date. (change)","answers":["changing"],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["changing","change","changed"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She admitted ___ the date. (change)","answers":["changing"],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to"},{"id":"en-b2-11-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["She admitted changing the date."],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","tokens":["She","admitted","changing","the","date."]},{"id":"en-b2-11-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"They suggested to check the records.","answers":["They suggested checking the records."],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to"},{"id":"en-b2-11-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["tan olmoq","rad etmoq","aniqlashtirmoq","bayon"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","left":["admit","deny","clarify","account"],"options":["tan olmoq","rad etmoq","aniqlashtirmoq","bayon"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reporting: “I changed the date,” she said, accepting responsibility.","answers":["She admitted changing the date."],"hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause."},{"id":"en-b2-11-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["The original verb distorted the statement.","The recording supports more neutral wording.","Preserve intention when reporting speech."],"answers":["The original verb distorted the statement.\nThe recording supports more neutral wording.\nPreserve intention when reporting speech."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"A meeting summary said that one student admitted hiding a file. The student had only said that she moved it to another folder. The writer had chosen a reporting verb that added a judgement unsupported by the statement. After checking the recording, the group rewrote the sentence neutrally. Another student did apologise for sending the wrong link, so that verb was justified. The teacher warned everyone not to publish names before the facts were checked. Reporting verbs can make a summary concise, but they must preserve the speaker’s intention. A strong verb is not automatically a more accurate verb. The revised account separates acknowledged mistakes, suggestions, and disputed claims rather than turning all of them into confessions.","sentences":["A meeting summary said that one student admitted hiding a file.","The student had only said that she moved it to another folder.","The writer had chosen a reporting verb that added a judgement unsupported by the statement.","After checking the recording, the group rewrote the sentence neutrally.","Another student did apologise for sending the wrong link, so that verb was justified.","The teacher warned everyone not to publish names before the facts were checked.","Reporting verbs can make a summary concise, but they must preserve the speaker’s intention.","A strong verb is not automatically a more accurate verb.","The revised account separates acknowledged mistakes, suggestions, and disputed claims rather than turning all of them into confessions."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-11-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Birinchi summary xatosi?","answers":["the verb added unsupported judgement"],"explanation":"Admitted hiding aytilmagan talqin.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["the verb added unsupported judgement","it was too neutral","the file never existed"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Qaysi verb asoslangan?","answers":["apologised for sending the wrong link"],"explanation":"U haqiqatan uzr so‘ragan.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["apologised for sending the wrong link","admitted hiding","confessed stealing"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["A meeting summary said that one student admitted hiding a file.","The student had only said that she moved it to another folder.","The writer had chosen a reporting verb that added a judgement unsupported by the statement.","After checking the recording, the group rewrote the sentence neutrally.","Another student did apologise for sending the wrong link, so that verb was justified.","The teacher warned everyone not to publish names before the facts were checked.","Reporting verbs can make a summary concise, but they must preserve the speaker’s intention.","A strong verb is not automatically a more accurate verb.","The revised account separates acknowledged mistakes, suggestions, and disputed claims rather than turning all of them into confessions."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is account. A meeting summary said that one student admitted hiding a file. The student had only said that she moved it to another folder. Speaker two: My main point is accuracy. The summary needs accuracy rather than the strongest possible verb. A meeting summary said that one student admitted hiding a file. The student had only said that she moved it to another folder. The writer had chosen a reporting verb that added a judgement unsupported by the statement. After checking the recording, the group rewrote the sentence neutrally. Another student did apologise for sending the wrong link, so that verb was justified. The teacher warned everyone not to publish names before the facts were checked. Reporting verbs can make a summary concise, but they must preserve the speaker’s intention. A strong verb is not automatically a more accurate verb. The revised account separates acknowledged mistakes, suggestions, and disputed claims rather than turning all of them into confessions.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-11.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-11-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Birinchi summary xatosi?","answers":["the verb added unsupported judgement"],"explanation":"Admitted hiding aytilmagan talqin.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["the verb added unsupported judgement","it was too neutral","the file never existed"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Qaysi verb asoslangan?","answers":["apologised for sending the wrong link"],"explanation":"U haqiqatan uzr so‘ragan.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["apologised for sending the wrong link","admitted hiding","confessed stealing"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["account","accuracy"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["The teacher warned us not to publish names."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-11-dictation.mp3","transcript":"The teacher warned us not to publish names."}]},"writing":{"task":"Neytral bayon yozing; uch reporting verb uchun aniq aytilgan gapni dalil qiling.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":320,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"The group reviewed the file incident and corrected its first summary. Lola said she had moved the file; she did not admit hiding it. Ali apologised for sending the wrong link, and the teacher warned everyone not to publish names before checking the facts. The group suggested reviewing the recording and agreed to update the notice. These verbs represent different actions and should not be treated as interchangeable. A fair summary preserves what speakers accepted, disputed, or proposed without adding unsupported judgement.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["She admitted changing the date.","He denied sharing the file.","They suggested checking the records."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Neytral bayon yozing; uch reporting verb uchun aniq aytilgan gapni dalil qiling. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":100,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Neytral bayon yozing; uch reporting verb uchun aniq aytilgan gapni dalil qiling.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b2-11-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She admitted ___ the date. (change)","answers":["changing"],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to"},{"id":"en-b2-11-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"He agreed ___ correct it.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to"},{"id":"en-b2-11-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"She apologised for ___ it. (send)","answers":["sending"],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to"},{"id":"en-b2-11-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Birinchi summary xatosi?","answers":["the verb added unsupported judgement"],"explanation":"Admitted hiding aytilmagan talqin.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["the verb added unsupported judgement","it was too neutral","the file never existed"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Qaysi verb asoslangan?","answers":["apologised for sending the wrong link"],"explanation":"U haqiqatan uzr so‘ragan.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["apologised for sending the wrong link","admitted hiding","confessed stealing"]}],[{"id":"en-b2-11-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["He denied sharing the file."],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","tokens":["He","denied","sharing","the","file."]},{"id":"en-b2-11-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"He agreed ___ correct it.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to"},{"id":"en-b2-11-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The teacher warned us not to publish names."],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","tokens":["The","teacher","warned","us","not","to","publish","names."]},{"id":"en-b2-11-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Birinchi summary xatosi?","answers":["the verb added unsupported judgement"],"explanation":"Admitted hiding aytilmagan talqin.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["the verb added unsupported judgement","it was too neutral","the file never existed"]},{"id":"en-b2-11-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["She apologised for sending the wrong link."],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","tokens":["She","apologised","for","sending","the","wrong","link."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b2-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b2-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b2-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b2-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b2-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b2-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b2-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b2-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b2-12','en-b2-12',null,4,12,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b2-12","baseId":"en-b2-12","revision":1,"level":"B2","levelIndex":4,"order":12,"title":"Non-defining relative clauses","objective":"Qo‘shimcha izohni shaxsni aniqlovchi ma’lumotdan ajratasiz.","context":"Non-defining relative clauses","prerequisites":["en-b2-11"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi.","Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi.","The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi."],"pattern":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","examples":["Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us.","The hall, which opened last year, is busy.","My neighbour, whose son studies here, helped.","The guide, whom we met yesterday, returned.","We visited Bukhara, where my aunt lives.","The printer stopped, which delayed the display."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b2-12-v0","term":"additional","meaning":"qo‘shimcha","ipa":"/əˈdɪʃənəl/","collocation":"additional information","example":"Grammar helps readers distinguish essential identification from additional background, rather than simply making sentences longer."},{"id":"en-b2-12-v1","term":"identify","meaning":"aniqlamoq","ipa":"/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/","collocation":"identify a person","example":"That detail is interesting but not necessary to identify the hall in this context."},{"id":"en-b2-12-v2","term":"omit","meaning":"tushirib qoldirmoq","ipa":"/əˈmɪt/","collocation":"omit a pronoun","example":"omit a pronoun"},{"id":"en-b2-12-v3","term":"distinction","meaning":"farq","ipa":"/dɪˈstɪŋkʃən/","collocation":"a meaning distinction","example":"a meaning distinction"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us.","The hall, which opened last year, is busy."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["Only a subgroup arrived early.","Five students appear in the record.","Use defining information to identify that subgroup."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"The guide, whom we met yesterday, returned.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-12-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b2-12-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: Lola, ___ leads the club, welcomed us.","answers":["who"],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["who","which","where"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Lola, ___ leads the club, welcomed us.","answers":["who"],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …"},{"id":"en-b2-12-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us."],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","tokens":["Lola,","who","leads","the","club,","welcomed","us."]},{"id":"en-b2-12-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Lola, that leads the club, welcomed us.","answers":["Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us."],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …"},{"id":"en-b2-12-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["qo‘shimcha","aniqlamoq","tushirib qoldirmoq","farq"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","left":["additional","identify","omit","distinction"],"options":["qo‘shimcha","aniqlamoq","tushirib qoldirmoq","farq"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Qo‘shimcha clause: Lola leads the club. Lola welcomed us.","answers":["Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us."],"hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi."},{"id":"en-b2-12-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["Only a subgroup arrived early.","Five students appear in the record.","Use defining information to identify that subgroup."],"answers":["Only a subgroup arrived early.\nFive students appear in the record.\nUse defining information to identify that subgroup."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."},{"id":"en-b2-12-collocations","type":"collocation","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni darsdagi birikmasi bilan moslang.","left":["additional","identify","omit","distinction"],"options":["additional information","identify a person","omit a pronoun","a meaning distinction"],"answers":["additional information","identify a person","omit a pronoun","a meaning distinction"],"hint":"So‘z qaysi birikmada ishlatilishini eslang.","explanation":"Birikmani yozgan gapingizda ham ishlating."},{"id":"en-b2-12-dialogue","type":"dialogue","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Sherik: “Can you give one example?” Siz: darsdagi birinchi namunani qayta tuzing.","answers":["Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us."],"tokens":["Lola,","who","leads","the","club,","welcomed","us."],"hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi."},{"id":"en-b2-12-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Reporting passive: Til vositasini tanlang: The centre is expected ___ reopen.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["to","for","at"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Reporting passive"},{"id":"en-b2-12-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Causative have va get: Til vositasini tanlang: I had my laptop ___. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["repaired","repairing","repair"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Causative have va get"},{"id":"en-b2-12-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Reporting verbs va mas’uliyat: Til vositasini tanlang: She admitted ___ the date. (change)","answers":["changing"],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["changing","change","changed"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Reporting verbs va mas’uliyat"}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"Two notices describe a club visit. One says that the students who arrived early helped arrange chairs. The other says that the students, who arrived early, helped arrange chairs. The first identifies a subgroup; the second adds information about the whole group already being discussed. A small punctuation change therefore changes the claim. Lola, who leads the club, asks the writer to check which meaning matches the attendance record. Only five students arrived early, so the first notice is accurate. The revised report also names the hall, which opened last year. That detail is interesting but not necessary to identify the hall in this context. Grammar helps readers distinguish essential identification from additional background, rather than simply making sentences longer.","sentences":["Two notices describe a club visit.","One says that the students who arrived early helped arrange chairs.","The other says that the students, who arrived early, helped arrange chairs.","The first identifies a subgroup; the second adds information about the whole group already being discussed.","A small punctuation change therefore changes the claim.","Lola, who leads the club, asks the writer to check which meaning matches the attendance record.","Only five students arrived early, so the first notice is accurate.","The revised report also names the hall, which opened last year.","That detail is interesting but not necessary to identify the hall in this context.","Grammar helps readers distinguish essential identification from additional background, rather than simply making sentences longer."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-12-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Birinchi notice kimlarni ajratadi?","answers":["the early-arriving subgroup"],"explanation":"Defining clause kichik guruh.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["the early-arriving subgroup","every student","the whole town"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Record qaysi gapni asoslaydi?","answers":["the version without commas"],"explanation":"Faqat beshta erta kelgan.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["the version without commas","the version with commas","neither because nobody arrived"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["Two notices describe a club visit.","One says that the students who arrived early helped arrange chairs.","The other says that the students, who arrived early, helped arrange chairs.","The first identifies a subgroup; the second adds information about the whole group already being discussed.","A small punctuation change therefore changes the claim.","Lola, who leads the club, asks the writer to check which meaning matches the attendance record.","Only five students arrived early, so the first notice is accurate.","The revised report also names the hall, which opened last year.","That detail is interesting but not necessary to identify the hall in this context.","Grammar helps readers distinguish essential identification from additional background, rather than simply making sentences longer."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is distinction. Two notices describe a club visit. One says that the students who arrived early helped arrange chairs. Speaker two: My main point is subgroup. The attendance record supports a subgroup rather than a claim about everyone. Two notices describe a club visit. One says that the students who arrived early helped arrange chairs. The other says that the students, who arrived early, helped arrange chairs. The first identifies a subgroup; the second adds information about the whole group already being discussed. A small punctuation change therefore changes the claim. Lola, who leads the club, asks the writer to check which meaning matches the attendance record. Only five students arrived early, so the first notice is accurate. The revised report also names the hall, which opened last year. That detail is interesting but not necessary to identify the hall in this context. Grammar helps readers distinguish essential identification from additional background, rather than simply making sentences longer.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-12.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-12-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Birinchi notice kimlarni ajratadi?","answers":["the early-arriving subgroup"],"explanation":"Defining clause kichik guruh.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["the early-arriving subgroup","every student","the whole town"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Record qaysi gapni asoslaydi?","answers":["the version without commas"],"explanation":"Faqat beshta erta kelgan.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["the version without commas","the version with commas","neither because nobody arrived"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["distinction","subgroup"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["The guide, whom we met yesterday, returned."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-12-dictation.mp3","transcript":"The guide, whom we met yesterday, returned."}]},"writing":{"task":"Visit reportda bir defining va ikki non-defining clause ishlating; guruh chegarasini izohlang.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":320,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"The students who arrived early helped arrange the chairs. Only five students were present at that time, so the report should not imply that the whole group arrived early. Lola, who leads the club, checked the attendance record before publishing the notice. The visit took place in the hall, which opened last year. This detail provides background without identifying a different hall. Our wording separates the subgroup that performed the task from additional information about people and places already known to the reader.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us.","The hall, which opened last year, is busy.","My neighbour, whose son studies here, helped."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Visit reportda bir defining va ikki non-defining clause ishlating; guruh chegarasini izohlang. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":100,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Visit reportda bir defining va ikki non-defining clause ishlating; guruh chegarasini izohlang.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b2-12-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Lola, ___ leads the club, welcomed us.","answers":["who"],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …"},{"id":"en-b2-12-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The hall, ___ opened last year, is busy.","answers":["which"],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …"},{"id":"en-b2-12-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"My neighbour, ___ son studies here, helped.","answers":["whose"],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …"},{"id":"en-b2-12-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Birinchi notice kimlarni ajratadi?","answers":["the early-arriving subgroup"],"explanation":"Defining clause kichik guruh.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["the early-arriving subgroup","every student","the whole town"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Record qaysi gapni asoslaydi?","answers":["the version without commas"],"explanation":"Faqat beshta erta kelgan.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["the version without commas","the version with commas","neither because nobody arrived"]}],[{"id":"en-b2-12-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The hall, which opened last year, is busy."],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","tokens":["The","hall,","which","opened","last","year,","is","busy."]},{"id":"en-b2-12-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The hall, ___ opened last year, is busy.","answers":["which"],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …"},{"id":"en-b2-12-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The guide, whom we met yesterday, returned."],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","tokens":["The","guide,","whom","we","met","yesterday,","returned."]},{"id":"en-b2-12-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Birinchi notice kimlarni ajratadi?","answers":["the early-arriving subgroup"],"explanation":"Defining clause kichik guruh.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","options":["the early-arriving subgroup","every student","the whole town"]},{"id":"en-b2-12-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The printer stopped, which delayed the display."],"explanation":"Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi. Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi. The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.","hint":"Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …","tokens":["T