tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b2-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b2-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b2-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b2-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied.","recapQuestions":[{"id":"en-b2-12-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Reporting passive: Til vositasini tanlang: The centre is expected ___ reopen.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi. Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved. Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.","hint":"It is reported that / is believed to have","options":["to","for","at"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Reporting passive"},{"id":"en-b2-12-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Causative have va get: Til vositasini tanlang: I had my laptop ___. (repair)","answers":["repaired"],"explanation":"Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan. Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi. Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.","hint":"have a device repaired / get someone to check it","options":["repaired","repairing","repair"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Causative have va get"},{"id":"en-b2-12-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Reporting verbs va mas’uliyat: Til vositasini tanlang: She admitted ___ the date. (change)","answers":["changing"],"explanation":"Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause. Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing. Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.","hint":"admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to","options":["changing","change","changed"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Reporting verbs va mas’uliyat"}]}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b2-13','en-b2-13',null,4,13,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b2-13","baseId":"en-b2-13","revision":1,"level":"B2","levelIndex":4,"order":13,"title":"Reduced relative va participle clauses","objective":"Qisqartirilgan gaplarda bajaruvchi mosligini tekshirasiz.","context":"Reduced relative va participle clauses","prerequisites":["en-b2-12"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no.","Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak.","Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating."],"pattern":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","examples":["Students waiting outside need tickets.","The reports written yesterday are ready.","Having checked the list, we opened the door.","Walking home, I noticed the rain.","Built last year, the hall is modern.","Not knowing the answer, she asked for help."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b2-13-v0","term":"reduce","meaning":"qisqartirmoq","ipa":"/rɪˈdjuːs/","collocation":"reduce a clause","example":"reduce a clause"},{"id":"en-b2-13-v1","term":"subject","meaning":"ega","ipa":"/ˈsʌbdʒɪkt/","collocation":"a shared subject","example":"She changes it to “Entering the hall, I noticed the bright lights.” The action now has a clear subject."},{"id":"en-b2-13-v2","term":"sequence","meaning":"ketma-ketlik","ipa":"/ˈsiːkwəns/","collocation":"an action sequence","example":"an action sequence"},{"id":"en-b2-13-v3","term":"ambiguity","meaning":"noaniqlik","ipa":"/ˌæmbɪˈɡjuːəti/","collocation":"avoid ambiguity","example":"avoid ambiguity"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["waiting outside / written recently / having checked","Students waiting outside need tickets.","The reports written yesterday are ready."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["Concision must preserve the subject.","Expanding the clause reveals who acts.","Shorten only when meaning remains clear."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"Walking home, I noticed the rain.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-13-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b2-13-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: Students ___ outside need tickets. (wait)","answers":["waiting"],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["waiting","wait","waited"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Students ___ outside need tickets. (wait)","answers":["waiting"],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked"},{"id":"en-b2-13-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["Students waiting outside need tickets."],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","tokens":["Students","waiting","outside","need","tickets."]},{"id":"en-b2-13-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Walking home, the rain began.","answers":["Walking home, I noticed that the rain began."],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked"},{"id":"en-b2-13-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["qisqartirmoq","ega","ketma-ketlik","noaniqlik"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","left":["reduce","subject","sequence","ambiguity"],"options":["qisqartirmoq","ega","ketma-ketlik","noaniqlik"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Qisqartiring: Students who are waiting outside need tickets.","answers":["Students waiting outside need tickets."],"hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no."},{"id":"en-b2-13-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["Concision must preserve the subject.","Expanding the clause reveals who acts.","Shorten only when meaning remains clear."],"answers":["Concision must preserve the subject.\nExpanding the clause reveals who acts.\nShorten only when meaning remains clear."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"A student tries to make a report shorter: “Entering the hall, the lights were bright.” The sentence seems to make the lights enter the hall. She changes it to “Entering the hall, I noticed the bright lights.” The action now has a clear subject. Another sentence describes reports written yesterday; here the reports receive the action, so the past participle is appropriate. Concision can make a report easier to read, but it is useful only when the relation between actions stays clear. The editor checks each shortened clause by expanding it. If the expanded version names a different subject or changes active to passive meaning, the shortening needs revision. Saving a few words is not worth making readers guess who did what.","sentences":["A student tries to make a report shorter: “Entering the hall, the lights were bright.","” The sentence seems to make the lights enter the hall.","She changes it to “Entering the hall, I noticed the bright lights.","” The action now has a clear subject.","Another sentence describes reports written yesterday; here the reports receive the action, so the past participle is appropriate.","Concision can make a report easier to read, but it is useful only when the relation between actions stays clear.","The editor checks each shortened clause by expanding it.","If the expanded version names a different subject or changes active to passive meaning, the shortening needs revision.","Saving a few words is not worth making readers guess who did what."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-13-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Birinchi gapda muammo?","answers":["the implied subject is wrong"],"explanation":"Kirayotgan ega noto‘g‘ri.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["the implied subject is wrong","all participles are banned","lights are never bright"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Qisqartirishni qanday tekshiradi?","answers":["expand the clause and compare meaning"],"explanation":"Expanded clause aloqa tekshiruvi.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["expand the clause and compare meaning","delete all subjects","count words only"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["A student tries to make a report shorter: “Entering the hall, the lights were bright.","” The sentence seems to make the lights enter the hall.","She changes it to “Entering the hall, I noticed the bright lights.","” The action now has a clear subject.","Another sentence describes reports written yesterday; here the reports receive the action, so the past participle is appropriate.","Concision can make a report easier to read, but it is useful only when the relation between actions stays clear.","The editor checks each shortened clause by expanding it.","If the expanded version names a different subject or changes active to passive meaning, the shortening needs revision.","Saving a few words is not worth making readers guess who did what."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is subject. A student tries to make a report shorter: “Entering the hall, the lights were bright. ” The sentence seems to make the lights enter the hall. Speaker two: My main point is clarity. A shorter sentence is useful only when its subject remains clear. A student tries to make a report shorter: “Entering the hall, the lights were bright.” The sentence seems to make the lights enter the hall. She changes it to “Entering the hall, I noticed the bright lights.” The action now has a clear subject. Another sentence describes reports written yesterday; here the reports receive the action, so the past participle is appropriate. Concision can make a report easier to read, but it is useful only when the relation between actions stays clear. The editor checks each shortened clause by expanding it. If the expanded version names a different subject or changes active to passive meaning, the shortening needs revision. Saving a few words is not worth making readers guess who did what.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-13.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b2-13-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Birinchi gapda muammo?","answers":["the implied subject is wrong"],"explanation":"Kirayotgan ega noto‘g‘ri.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["the implied subject is wrong","all participles are banned","lights are never bright"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Qisqartirishni qanday tekshiradi?","answers":["expand the clause and compare meaning"],"explanation":"Expanded clause aloqa tekshiruvi.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["expand the clause and compare meaning","delete all subjects","count words only"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["subject","clarity"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["Walking home, I noticed the rain."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b2-13-dictation.mp3","transcript":"Walking home, I noticed the rain."}]},"writing":{"task":"Reportning uch gapini qisqartirib, ega va active/passive ma’nosini izohlang.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":320,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"Having checked the attendance list, we opened the hall to visitors. Students waiting outside were given tickets in order of arrival. The reports written yesterday were displayed near the entrance. These shortened clauses reduce repetition while keeping the actions clear. In the first sentence, we both checked the list and opened the hall. In the second, students do the waiting. In the third, reports receive the writing action. When editing, I expanded each clause to make sure the shorter version preserved the original meaning.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["Students waiting outside need tickets.","The reports written yesterday are ready.","Having checked the list, we opened the door."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Reportning uch gapini qisqartirib, ega va active/passive ma’nosini izohlang. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":100,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Reportning uch gapini qisqartirib, ega va active/passive ma’nosini izohlang.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b2-13-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Students ___ outside need tickets. (wait)","answers":["waiting"],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked"},{"id":"en-b2-13-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reports ___ yesterday are ready. (write)","answers":["written"],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked"},{"id":"en-b2-13-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Having ___ the list, we opened the door. (check)","answers":["checked"],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked"},{"id":"en-b2-13-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Birinchi gapda muammo?","answers":["the implied subject is wrong"],"explanation":"Kirayotgan ega noto‘g‘ri.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["the implied subject is wrong","all participles are banned","lights are never bright"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Qisqartirishni qanday tekshiradi?","answers":["expand the clause and compare meaning"],"explanation":"Expanded clause aloqa tekshiruvi.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["expand the clause and compare meaning","delete all subjects","count words only"]}],[{"id":"en-b2-13-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The reports written yesterday are ready."],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","tokens":["The","reports","written","yesterday","are","ready."]},{"id":"en-b2-13-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Reports ___ yesterday are ready. (write)","answers":["written"],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked"},{"id":"en-b2-13-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Walking home, I noticed the rain."],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","tokens":["Walking","home,","I","noticed","the","rain."]},{"id":"en-b2-13-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Birinchi gapda muammo?","answers":["the implied subject is wrong"],"explanation":"Kirayotgan ega noto‘g‘ri.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","options":["the implied subject is wrong","all participles are banned","lights are never bright"]},{"id":"en-b2-13-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Not knowing the answer, she asked for help."],"explanation":"Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no. Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak. Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.","hint":"waiting outside / written recently / having checked","tokens":["Not","knowing","the","answer,","she","asked","for","help."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b2-13","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b2-13","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b2-13","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://le